https://gist.github.com/jcheng5/6604738
shiny::runGist("https://gist.github.com/jcheng5/6604738")

I think the main problem is that the find() reactive was serving too many purposes. I found it much easier to break it up into different jobs.

I also changed the problem around so that selecting a choices from the selectInput put the corresponding value into the textInput. I think that is more clear to the user anyway.

The other thing you might try is looking into select2 <http://ivaynberg.github.io/select2/>. We don't have an "official" binding for this--yet--but some folks in the group have tinkered with it.
https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/shiny-discuss/select2

